# docker/base-images.env — T0.7.2
#
# Digest-pinned Node base images consumed by every app Dockerfile
# (apps/{api,worker,web}/Dockerfile) via `ARG NODE_BASE` / `ARG
# NODE_RUNTIME_BASE`. A floating tag (`node:24-alpine`) means two builds of
# the same commit can pull different underlying layers on different days —
# that turns "works on my machine" into a Kubernetes rollback nobody can
# reproduce. Pinning by digest makes the base image itself part of the
# commit, not a moving target resolved at build time.
#
# <major> is 24, from .nvmrc. Both vars point at the SAME node:24-alpine
# digest today — alpine is already the minimal Node base Docker Hub
# publishes (there's no separate "slim"/distroless Node image the way
# there is for e.g. python:slim), and the multi-stage Dockerfiles
# (T0.7.4-6) already discard every build-time tool — the pnpm store, dev
# dependencies, the turbo/pruner stage — before the runtime stage. A
# second, smaller runtime base would buy nothing further today. If a
# slimmer official Node base ever ships, split these two vars then.
#
# Each digest is the OCI *manifest-list* (multi-arch index) digest:
#   docker buildx imagetools inspect node:24-alpine --format '{{.Manifest.Digest}}'
# NOT a single-platform manifest digest — pinning the list keeps the image
# multi-arch (amd64 dev laptops and CI, arm64 for e.g. Graviton runners)
# instead of silently freezing to whichever architecture happened to
# resolve the digest first.
#
# Never hand-edit the digest below — run scripts/refresh-base-digests.sh
# to re-resolve it deliberately (it rewrites this file AND the matching
# `ARG NODE_BASE=...` / `ARG NODE_RUNTIME_BASE=...` default lines in every
# apps/*/Dockerfile, so all four files stay in lockstep). Run it with
# --check as a drift guard: it exits non-zero if the registry now serves a
# different digest for the same tag than what's pinned here, without
# writing anything.

NODE_BASE=node:24-alpine@sha256:a0b9bf06e4e6193cf7a0f58816cc935ff8c2a908f81e6f1a95432d679c54fbfd
NODE_RUNTIME_BASE=node:24-alpine@sha256:a0b9bf06e4e6193cf7a0f58816cc935ff8c2a908f81e6f1a95432d679c54fbfd
